    {
      "id": "C-b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 78,
      "y": 2644,
      "width": 561,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1048551390,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1186845503,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795161628189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "const asyncHandler = (controller) => (req, res, next) => {\n  Promise.resolve(controller(req, res)).catch(next);\n};",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "const asyncHandler = (controller) => (req, res, next) => {\n  Promise.resolve(controller(req, res)).catch(next);\n};",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b10"
    },
    {
      "id": "C-res",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2734,
      "width": 1198,
      "height": 43,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1277844000,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1797997617,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795161628189,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The wrapper returns nothing, so Express sees no promise. .catch(next) is the manual hand-off: rejection → next(err) ✔\nThis is why asyncHandler exists here: it works regardless of how Express handles returned promises.",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The wrapper returns nothing, so Express sees no promise. .catch(next) is the manual hand-off: rejection → next(err) ✔\nThis is why asyncHandler exists here: it works regardless of how Express handles returned promises.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b11"
    },
